# T5a step 6: the joiner half of "stop, author while absent, restart,
# converge" (design_docs/2026-07-28_turnstone_place_port_plan.md, "T5a",
# Scope). Runs as a SECOND process against the SAME appdata/root/profile the
# phase-1 joiner used (scenarios/place_joiner.scn), so the place binding,
# rendezvous and stores the worker persisted are retained offline at startup.
# Paired with the founder's phase-2 continuation in scenarios/place_founder.scn
# through the shared ${EXCHANGE} directory and ${FOUNDER_DIR} (the founder's
# capture dir, passed by scenarios/place_two_windows.ps1).
settle 30
key escape

# Retained history is visible immediately at startup, before any reconnect:
# the worker persisted place.json/place-rendezvous.json/place/ under
# TURNSTONE_ROOT and current_session points at it, so this is an offline
# reopen, not a fresh join.
wait-status 600 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 2 messages

# A "Reconnect place" issued right after a live open in the SAME process is
# refused (store still locked); this IS the real restart that makes it valid.
act Reconnect place
settle 5
wait-status 600 Local rendezvous

# Wait for the founder's absent-authored message (written while this joiner
# was stopped) before expecting it to have converged.
wait-file 6000 ${FOUNDER_DIR}\founder_absent_authored.json
wait-status 3000 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 3 messages

act Send place message
settle 5
type back again
key enter
settle 10
wait-status 600 Retained history: 0 shared nodes, 4 messages

# Signal the founder that the return leg is complete; T5b step 4 continues
# from here (design_docs/2026-07-28_turnstone_place_port_plan.md, "T5b.
# Shared address and refused write") — the founder invites the reader and
# shares a node on the address below while this process waits for it.
touch ${EXCHANGE}\joiner.returned

# The founder's shared node arrives through ordinary graph sync, no local
# action needed beyond waiting for the retained-history count to grow.
wait-status 6000 Retained history: 1 shared nodes

# Opening the same address selects the already-synced (reconciled) node
# rather than minting a second local one: the node count must not grow
# across the open.
assert nodes == 1
open ${EXCHANGE_URL}/shared.html
settle 20
assert nodes == 1
# Live content is per node and off until asked for; the presented Reader in
# the workbench is the shared address's live web surface (reframe step 4).
act Toggle live content
settle 30
assert content-ready
assert content-live
act Open node in Workbench
settle 30
assert pane workbench
assert surface content
capture joiner_shared

# T5c: visit the founder's shared Knot document by projection (design_docs/
# 2026-07-28_turnstone_place_port_plan.md, "T5c"). The founder shares it
# after the reader's leg completes, so this profile's shared-node count goes
# from 1 to 2; the exact knot:// address (holder root hex) is never known to
# this scenario in advance, so the node is found and opened by its Roster
# row rather than by address. The Roster (not Trail) is the pane that lists
# every graph node regardless of local navigation history: a node that
# arrived purely through sync (never separately visited/opened here) shows
# up there but not in Trail's recent/history rows (run 17 found trail/roster/
# inspector/arrange all reporting empty because no list pane was open yet).
wait-status 6000 Retained history: 2 shared nodes
act Open Roster pane
settle 5
wait-row 600 field.knot
click-row field.knot
settle 20
act Toggle live content
wait
assert content-live
# Present it in the Workbench, same as the shared HTML page above and as the
# founder's own leg: `insert` needs an addressable content surface, which
# opening/toggling alone does not provide (run 17).
act Open node in Workbench
settle 20
assert pane workbench
assert surface content
wait-knot 600 visiting

# Content focus is set only by a real pointer press on the surface, so the
# editor is pressed at its tile: with the Roster open on the right, the Knot
# tile sits between the shared page and the Roster (see joiner_knot_page.png).
capture joiner_knot_page
click-at 700 110
settle 10
key end
key space
insert joiner revision
key ctrl+s
wait
assert text saved
touch ${EXCHANGE}\joiner.edited

# The founder authors its own revision only after seeing this edit; wait for
# its marker, then wait for the projection to actually deliver that edit to
# this visiting session before comparing text.
wait-file 6000 ${EXCHANGE}\founder.edited
wait
settle 300
assert text founder revision
record-place joiner_knot
capture joiner_knot
touch ${EXCHANGE}\knot.done

# The founder process exits once it sees knot.done above, which is what
# takes the holder away; wait for this session's own view of that.
wait-knot 6000 unavailable
capture joiner_unavailable

act Place status
settle 10
capture joiner_return
record-place joiner_return

log joiner return path complete
